{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/543155-question-about-soul-pacts","id":543155,"title":"Question About Soul Pacts....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-06T15:56:44-07:00","id":543155,"title":"Question About Soul Pacts....","content":"Trought pacts a demon can stole assets and acquaintances to humans and add them to it's own cover. But what appens when a soul pact is sealed and a human gives away his whole existence? Effects are immediate? Or is up to the demon settle when the soul pact becomes effective? And there's something else I don't understand: where's the profit for the human contraent in selling his own life? When performing a pact a demon is not allowed to cheat the other counterpart, then why a human should agree to seal a such deal, putting his existence at risk?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T16:51:30-07:00","id":543229,"title":"","content":"When a soul pact is sealed, the demon is permitted to claim it and consume the signatory as a Cover at any time (unless the agreed terms of the pact add restrictions) by touching the signatory.<br /> <br /> Soul pacts are bad deals. Full stop. But demons aren't obligated to offer good deals; they're merely obligated to offer <i>honest</i> deals and refrain from supernatural compulsion in the negotiation. You can, however, use any degree of physical force or threats of supernatural force you like short of physically grabbing their hand and signing the document for them.<br /> <br /> You can offer to do something they can't do, something they're so desperate for that it's worth their life. I don't care if you kill me, as long as you can take my daughter to a safe place and make sure she gets an upbringing full of love.<br /> <br /> You can find \u2014 or <i>put</i> \u2014 somebody in a situation where annihilation is a preferable way to go. Better to fade away than face the Hell that's waiting for me after all I've done. Or, they say it's terminal and the pain is already awful, but if you say you can do some good in my shoes in with the time left over... Or, if you sign this paper I can promise you I won't ever do anything to harm your family, but if you don't sign, then things start to get cloudy, see?<br /> <br /> You can rush and pressure the signatory to sign, distracting them with ambiguous language before they consider and pay attention to the terms you've laid out before them. Now I won't lie, the devil's in the details here, but yada yada, the short of what it means is it says your wife will have her husband by her side to keep her safe as long as this happens, no matter how rough it gets. The window's narrowing, though. This is a limited time offer.<br /> <br /> You can set creative conditions to the terms of the pact that transform it into a gamble. Feeling confident? You say you have the idea of a lifetime if you could just get the right ear? How about a deal. You sign this paper and I start greasing the wheels, things start going your way. I take you to the finish line, but you need to cross it. If I take you all the way there and your pitch to the bigwigs flops? Then you're mine.<br /> <br /> Or you could just start beating the hell out of them until they read and sign the goddamn paper just to make it stop.<br /> <br /> Most of these options to achieve a soul pact are pretty evil or at least morally shady and callous. But, well. You're Unchained. This is a choice you face a lot. Easy, fast and clean: pick two. You never get all three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T17:37:22-07:00","id":543258,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the underlying theme of negotiating soul pacts it that the Demon is usually negotiating in bad faith. The Demon <i>knows</i> it will be a bad deal for the Human. Hence why the targets are often those who are desperate or blinded by their own arrogance. And if they're not desperate, it's quite easy for the Demon to make them desperate without any supernatural forces, whatsoever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T04:52:39-07:00","id":543747,"title":"","content":"Here's another angle. Who says the human understands what it means to sell their soul? For all the human knows, it just means the devil claims their ghost after they die, not that the demon can take over their life. There's a lot of misconceptions floating around about what things mean, and a demon can take full advantage of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-09T11:11:44-07:00","id":547349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/543155-question-about-soul-pacts#post543155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trought pacts a demon can stole assets and acquaintances to humans and add them to it's own cover. But what appens when a soul pact is sealed and a human gives away his whole existence? Effects are immediate? Or is up to the demon settle when the soul pact becomes effective? And there's something else I don't understand: where's the profit for the human contraent in selling his own life? When performing a pact a demon is not allowed to cheat the other counterpart, then why a human should agree to seal a such deal, putting his existence at risk?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that there's a really amazing extension of the Soul Pact system in the Demon Interfaces book. It allows more conditional pacts, and pacts that can be traded to other demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T14:46:47-07:00","id":549395,"title":"","content":"Tanks for answers! But now, what happens to a soul pact's cover when the demon switches to another one? The original human comes back?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T20:18:49-07:00","id":549634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/543155-question-about-soul-pacts?p=549395#post549395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tanks for answers! But now, what happens to a soul pact's cover when the demon switches to another one? The original human comes back?</div> </div> </div> </div>The cover is essentially in 'storage'. Once you've annihilated said human by calling in the pact and stepped into the breach, there's no going backwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-11T06:17:09-07:00","id":550052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/543155-question-about-soul-pacts?p=549395#post549395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tanks for answers! But now, what happens to a soul pact's cover when the demon switches to another one? The original human comes back?</div> </div> </div> </div> When you claim a soul, it becomes a new Cover. There is absolutely no difference between it, your original Cover, a patchwork job, or any other kind of Cover now. The human died when you claimed their soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T14:39:32-07:00","id":552186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/543155-question-about-soul-pacts?p=549395#post549395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tanks for answers! But now, what happens to a soul pact's cover when the demon switches to another one? The original human comes back?</div> </div> </div> </div>The human is destroyed, completely. You crumpled him up into a wad and made a hat out of him. Once you have the hat, you can fold all your hats up in your pocket and carry them around with you, and you can take off the hat you're wearing and put a different hat on. But they're just hats, not people anymore, just the appearance of people. You can't turn the hat back into a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}